e keeps protecting the credential where it can:`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`An entry in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`files`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`envVars`}),` that still has a valid `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`path`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`name`}),` and a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mode`}),` of `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mask`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`deny`}),`, such as one whose `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`extract`}),` pattern has no capturing group, is degraded to `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mode: \"deny\"`}),` with a warning, so the credential stays blocked, not masked, until you fix the entry. A degraded `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`files`}),` entry pins `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/sandboxing#disable-filesystem-isolation`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`filesystem.disabled`})}),` like an explicit `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`deny`}),` entry, and the warning notes that its read block isn’t enforced if managed settings turn filesystem isolation off.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`An entry with an unknown `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mode`}),` or an invalid `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`path`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`name`}),` is stripped.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`Each case warns; whether an entry is degraded or stripped, the remaining valid entries are still enforced, and a wholly invalid `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`credentials`}),` value is dropped while the rest of `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`sandbox`}),` still applies.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Applies in v2.1.191 and later; before v2.1.221, every invalid entry was stripped. For the other managed keys with per-field handling, see `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/managed-settings#invalid-entries-in-managed-settings`,children:`Invalid entries in managed settings`}),`.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`sandbox-credentials-files`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`sandbox.credentials.files`})}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Protect credential files or directories from sandboxed commands. With `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"mode\": \"deny\"`}),`, Claude Code blocks reads of the path inside the sandbox, the same read block as `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#sandbox-filesystem-denyread`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`sandbox.filesystem.denyRead`})}),`. With `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"mode\": \"mask\"`}),`, sandboxed commands on Linux and WSL2 read a sentinel copy of the file, and the sandbox proxy substitutes the real value on outbound requests to that entry’s `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`injectHosts`}),`; on macOS the file is unreadable inside the sandbox instead. Requires Claude Code v2.1.187 or later, and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"mode\": \"mask\"`}),` requires v2.1.221 or later.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Scope`}),`: `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#scopes`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`Any file`})}),`. Claude Code drops `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mask`}),` entries from project `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.claude/settings.json`}),` and local `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.claude/settings.local.json`}),`.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Type`}),`: array of objects, each with `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`path`}),` and a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mode`}),` of `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"deny\"`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"mask\"`}),`, plus the optional `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#mask-fields-for-files`,children:`mask fields for files`})]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Default`}),`: unset, so no credential files are protec