children:`\"deny\"`}),`, or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"error\"`}),`; default `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"warn\"`})]}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`What happens when `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`extract`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`decode`}),` finds nothing to mask. `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`warn`}),` leaves the file readable as-is inside the sandbox, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`deny`}),` makes it unreadable, and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`error`}),` stops sandbox setup until you fix the configuration. Claude Code treats `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`deny`}),` as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`error`}),` when the read block wouldn’t be enforced, because you `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/sandboxing#disable-filesystem-isolation`,children:`disable filesystem isolation`}),` or a `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#sandbox-filesystem-allowread`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`sandbox.filesystem.allowRead`})}),` entry re-opens the path. Requires v2.1.221 or later; the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`decode`}),` case requires v2.1.224 or later`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`decode`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`the string `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"jwt\"`})]}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Find JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) in the file, with a built-in pattern or with `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`extract`}),` when set, verify each candidate, and replace it with a structurally valid fake token, so code inside the sandbox that decodes the token keeps working. When no candidate verifies, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`onExtractNoMatch`}),` governs the outcome. Requires v2.1.224 or later`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{ch