jsx(_components.code,{children:`~/.claude/skills/`}),` plugin scan back in`]})]})]})]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Three source types carry rules beyond the table:`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`url`})}),`: a URL marketplace downloads only the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`marketplace.json`}),` file, not plugin files, so its plugins must use a `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/plugin-marketplaces#plugin-sources`,children:`plugin source`}),` other than a relative path. For plugins with relative paths, use a Git-based marketplace instead. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/plugin-marketplaces#plugins-with-relative-paths-fail-in-url-based-marketplaces`,children:`Plugins with relative paths fail in URL-based marketplaces`}),`.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`hostPattern`})}),`: use it to allow every marketplace on an internal GitHub Enterprise or GitLab server without listing each repository. Claude Code matches `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`github`}),` sources against `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`github.com`}),`, takes the hostname from `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`url`}),` sources, and takes it from `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`git`}),` sources depending on the `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://git-scm.com/docs/git-clone#_git_urls`,children:`git URL`}),`’s form:`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`A URL with a scheme, such as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`https://`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ssh://`}),`: the hostname in the URL.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`An SSH address without a scheme, in git’s `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`user@host:path`}),` form, such as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`git@git.example.com:tools/plugins.git`}),`: the host between `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`@`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`:`}),`, which is the host git connects to.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`Any other form without a scheme: no host, so no `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`strictKnownMarketplaces`}),` `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`hostPattern`}),` entry matches it. For a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`blockedMarketplaces`}),` `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`hostPattern`}),`, Claude Code takes a host from a wider set of forms, so a blocklist entry can still match such a form. Before v2.1.234, a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`strictKnownMarketplaces`}),` `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`hostPattern`}),` also matched some forms that git doesn’t treat as SSH addresses.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`file`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`directory`}),` sources have no host and never match a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`hostPattern`}),` entry.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`pathPattern`})}),`: use it to allow filesystem marketplaces alongside `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`hostPattern`}),` entries for network sources. `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\".*\"`}),` allows every local path; a narrower pattern such as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"^/opt/approved/\"`}),` restricts to a directory.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Any allowlist, even an empty one, also stops Claude Code loading `,_jsxs(_components.a,{href:`/en/plugins-reference#skills-directory-plugins`,children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`@skills-dir`}),` plugins`]}),` from `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`~/.claude/skills/`}),`. Add the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`{ \"source\": \"skills-dir\" }`}),` entry to keep loading them; the entry has no meaning outside this key and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`blockedMarketplaces`}),`.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`4`,id:`owner-wildcards`,children:`Owner wildcards`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`A `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`github`}),` entry whose `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`repo`}),` value is `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"\u003cowner\u003e/*\"`}),` matches every repository under that GitHub owner. Owner wildcards require Claude Code v2.1.223 or later and work only in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`strictKnownMarketplaces`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`blockedMarketplaces`}),`. Everywhere else a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`github`}),` source appears, such as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`extraKnownMarketplaces`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/plugin marketplace add`}),`, the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`repo`}),` value must name a single repository. Before v2.1.223, Claude Code compared the entry literally, so an allowlist entry matched no repository and a blocklist entry blocked nothing; single-repository entries are enforced on every version.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`This entry allows any marketplace repository in the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`acme-corp`}),` organization:`]}),`\n`,_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:`managed-settings.json`,numberOfLines:`5`,language:`json`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`json`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`json`,numberOfLines:`5`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:`{`})}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#116329`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#9CDCFE`},children:`  \"