pdates the file.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.li,{children:`If you set both spellings in one file, Claude Code uses the canonical value and ignores the alias.`}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`pluginconfigs`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`pluginConfigs`})}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Store the non-sensitive answers you give a plugin’s `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/plugins-reference#user-configuration`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`userConfig`})}),` configuration dialog, keyed by plugin ID. Claude Code writes this key to your user settings when you fill in the dialog, so you don’t need to edit it by hand. Sensitive options go to the macOS Keychain instead, or to `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`~/.claude/.credentials.json`}),` on platforms without a supported keychain.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Scope`}),`: `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#scopes`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`User or managed`})})]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Type`}),`: object mapping a plugin ID to an object with an `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`options`}),` field, mapping each option name to a string, number, Boolean, or array of strings, and an optional `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mcpServers`}),` field holding per-server user configuration values in the same shape`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Default`}),`: unset`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`This example stores the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`api_endpoint`}),` option for the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`deployer`}),` plugin from `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`acme-tools`}),`:`]}),`\n`,_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:`settings.json`,numberOfLines:`9`,language:`json`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`